 "note": [
  "Scripture authority is the 1962 Amharic Bible (UBS; NT revised 2003). Its New Testament is on disk whole (ebible mirror gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/amh_amh/usfm; re-verified for this job: all 27 NT books return 200, gen/psa/isa 404, and no other Amharic collection is in the mirror). The mirror carries no Old Testament, so OT quotations reuse the wording of the parent edition, watchman-nee-a-life.am.json, where it quotes the same verse, and are otherwise self_rendered in the 1962 register.",
  "A `mined` row was re-measured against the finished text: every segment (split at an elision …) is an exact substring of at least 20 characters of the 1962 NT, or of 25 characters of the cited corpus file. Shorter or re-personed quotations are self_rendered, whatever the translator believed. Several mirror entries are bridged and lossy (1 Cor 6:18-20 holds only v18, Eph 2:6-8 only v8), so 1 Cor 6:19-20 and Eph 2:6 take the parent edition's wording, which is the 1962 text.",
  "The English quotes the ASV; per the Amharic teens editions the epigraphs cite book and verse with no version label. Ezekiel 3:17 and Psalm 13:1 open with the parent edition's clause; their second halves have no shipped Amharic rendering and are self_rendered. Luke 1:46-47 is the 1962 v47, which carries both clauses in that Bible's division."
